  <data key="d5">1776983281</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noisy Neighbor Antipattern">
  <data key="d0">Noisy Neighbor Antipattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Noisy Neighbor antipattern occurs when shared resources cause performance degradation, mitigated by dedicated subscriptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoscaling">
  <data key="d0">Autoscaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscaling is a best practice method for automatically adjusting resources in response to load changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling is configured based on service-internal and application-set thresholds to respond to load-level volatility.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling balances workload supply against demand by dynamically adjusting resources, introducing variability and additional lifecycle events.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscaling automatically adjusts resources based on demand but can be misconfigured, leading to excess cost or uncontrolled growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AKS">
  <data key="d0">AKS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a managed Kubernetes platform on Azure that provides container orchestration capabilities. It supports cluster and node upgrades, networking, monitoring, and governance. AKS serves as a primary application platform and compute environment, using container images from container registries and allowing health endpoint configuration for pods.

AKS has a hard requirement for an underlying virtual network and requires network integration configuration. It supports both Azure CNI and Kubenet networking plugins, and can be optimized with accelerated networking for query-intensive workloads. The service has a scale limit of 1,000 nodes per cluster and is monitored for CPU utilization and deployment statuses.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) has a hard requirement for an underlying virtual network.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a managed Kubernetes service requiring network integration configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) is a managed Kubernetes service that supports Azure CNI and Kubenet networking plugins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5321cfe4fbc08d735ac5eac02e84e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active/Active Model">
  <data key="d0">Active/Active Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An active/active deployment strategy that maximizes availability and provides a higher composite SLA by distributing load among all regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The active/active model is a deployment strategy where load is distributed among all regions simultaneously to maximize resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;The active/active deployment model runs multiple regions simultaneously and is strongly recommended for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e07a49a74635d695d2a74e26e941143f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure SDKs">
  <data key="d0">Azure SDKs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SDKs are software development kits for Azure, available in multiple programming languages, with varying update frequencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Vendor-provided SDKs recommended for connecting to dependent Azure services, offering built-in resiliency capabilities.</data>
