<node id="Azure Cosmos DB">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB is a globally distributed, highly available NoSQL database service on the Azure platform. It is a PaaS offering that abstracts infrastructure complexity and automatically distributes workloads across instances, zones, and regions. It provides multi-region read and write capabilities, transparent replication, and conflict resolution options, and notably does not require automated failover configuration when multi-write deployment is enabled.

Azure Cosmos DB offers tunable consistency levels, multiple API support, Availability Zone redundancy, and configurable authentication methods including role-based access control. Built-in reliability features include partitioning, indexing, automatic backups with multiple backup modes (including periodic backup), and high-reliability SLAs for availability and throughput. SDK language support is also a key consideration. It is particularly recommended for applications spanning more than four deployment regions.

The service supports both transactional and analytical workloads. It features a change feed capability, an analytical column store, and built-in Time to Live (TTL) for managing data growth. The analytical store enables large-scale analytics without impacting transactional performance. Azure Cosmos DB integrates with Azure Synapse for big data analytics and is commonly used to store "hot" data actively used by applications.

From an operational perspective, Azure Cosmos DB server-side latency is tracked as a key monitoring metric. It is also commonly used as a downstream dependency within regional deployment stamps, serving as a primary data platform within many Azure architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB supports point-in-time restore with continuous backup.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB is a data platform used as an example of a downstream dependency within regional deployment stamps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36d66c785cc9b10b4cf377888b6bd59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8</data>
