<node id="Event-Driven Design">
  <data key="d0">Event-Driven Design</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design approach using asynchronous message processing through an intermediary to build resiliency and loose coupling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Tracing">
  <data key="d0">Distributed Tracing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A diagnostic approach for end-to-end tracing across services, providing correlation IDs and comprehensive error messages.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed Tracing is facilitated by Application Insights to provide comprehensive error messages with correlation IDs.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed Tracing is a diagnostic method facilitated by Application Insights for tracking requests across services.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed tracing is an observability technique whose complexity increases when additional reliability components are introduced into an architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed tracing correlates telemetry across critical system flows for end-to-end transaction insights and root cause analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Insights">
  <data key="d0">Application Insights</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Application Insights is an Application Performance Monitoring (APM) tool and a feature of Azure Monitor. It collects application logs, metrics, and traces, providing deep insights into application performance and application-related issues. It can be deployed in a workspace-based model underpinned by Log Analytics.

Application Insights facilitates Distributed Tracing and provides correlation IDs for error tracking. It helps users query, correlate, and visualize application traces. As an Azure Monitor resource, it must be deployed and configured to incorporate data collection and querying capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58687539bce004e3d6c298bc58bb0198</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure ExpressRoute">
  <data key="d0">Azure ExpressRoute</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A connectivity option for accessing workloads through private networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure ExpressRoute is a cloud connectivity solution that serves as a typical external dependency for workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981044</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loosely Coupled Event-Driven Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Loosely Coupled Event-Driven Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture where components operate independently via well-defined interfaces and asynchronous message processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outbox Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Outbox Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern used to guarantee consistency so that every message is processed correctly in distributed services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transactional Session">
  <data key="d0">Transactional Session</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A design pattern used alongside the Outbox pattern to guarantee message processing consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Model">
  <data key="d0">Health Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Health Model is a layered, iterative framework used to define, quantify, and aggregate the health of individual application components and the overall workload. It represents application health using traffic light states—Healthy, Degraded, and Unavailable—by defining healthy and unhealthy states for each component to enable fast failure detection and recovery.

The Health Model monitors application component health status through health endpoints, takes corrective action for non-transient failures, and spots early warning signs to trigger appropriate recovery processes based on defined disaster thresholds. It provides in-depth visibility into components and overall workload health as part of observability and reliability strategies.

The Health Model quantifies application health in the context of availability and performance requirements, measuring operational efficiency. It leverages key resource-level metrics and scoring functions, and can be integrated with alerts and CI/CD pipelines for calculating SLO attainment.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is a graphical representation of logical entities and their relationships for a given scope, where each node has a health state definition to rationalize monitoring data.&lt;SEP&gt;A model that provides operators visibility into system health, dependencies, and business impact, using a distinct data schema optimized for observability.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is a comprehensive framework that correlates various monitoring data to accurately reflect the runtime state of entities or an entire workload.&lt;SEP&gt;A health model is a framework for quantifying and visualizing the operational health states of workloads, applications, and infrastructure components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ed4331e930dc66a90d716e75ccb847e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a688a846e77a6107a53c8f43220265c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4aefadf5c38a99059d5cac5297d2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74ac1201f940bb7bb5693682e4dbc30b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d847dca2d14a4e01f2ac8a1fb0f3723</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-design.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Service">
  <data key="d0">App Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure App Service is a cloud platform for hosting web applications with features like autoscaling, per-app scaling, and diagnostic logging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Container Registry">
  <data key="d0">Azure Container Registry</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Container Registry is a service for storing and managing container images with geo-replication and vulnerability scanning capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is a native Azure service for hosting container images, supporting geo-replication, Microsoft Entra authentication, and automated container building.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is a container image registry that requires automated procedures for removing old image versions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Heal">
  <data key="d0">Auto Heal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Heal automatically recycles unhealthy workers to enable self-healing for mission-critical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Check">
  <data key="d0">Health Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Check identifies non-responsive workers by assessing critical downstream dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TCP Port Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">TCP Port Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TCP port exhaustion occurs when outbound connections from a given App Service worker exceed capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;TCP port exhaustion occurs when outbound connections from a worker exceed capacity, depending on worker size.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker Hub">
  <data key="d0">Docker Hub</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Docker Hub is a public container registry that can lead to issues with service availability, throttling, and data exfiltration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log Analytics">
  <data key="d0">Log Analytics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Log Analytics is an Azure service used for ingesting, storing, and querying operational data, including application-level and platform-level diagnostic logs. It serves as a destination for Azure Monitor operational data from resources such as Azure Cosmos DB and other global resources, and is used for auditing and logging in AKS to address security risks.

Log Analytics has query limits and pricing tiers that may require optimization, particularly around concurrent query limits. Its exported data can be ingested into Azure Synapse for AIOps analysis and queried via Synapse Spark.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics workspace serves as a global unified data sink for operational data from Azure Front Door.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics is an Azure tool used alongside Azure Monitor to detect issues in workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics workspace serves as a global unified data sink for operational data from Azure Front Door.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Event Hubs">
  <data key="d0">Azure Event Hubs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Event Hubs serves as a tool for ingesting diagnostic logs to third-party tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Hubs is an export destination for Log Analytics workspace data, required to be in the same region as the workspace.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Event Hubs is an Azure PaaS product with geo-disaster recovery capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Container Registry">
  <data key="d0">Container Registry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Container registries host images deployed to container runtime environments like AKS, requiring careful configuration for mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Container Registry is a service for hosting container images with support for geo-replication, zone redundancy, image locking, and private endpoints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Entra">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Entra</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Entra provides authentication capabilities for Azure Container Registry.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides integrated authentication for pushing and pulling container images.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides identity and role-based access control (RBAC) for Azure Cosmos DB authentication and resource management.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides authentication to connect to services without using connection strings or keys.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides custom roles used for authorization in a least privilege model for Key Vault operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Entra provides activity logs that can be exported to Log Analytics Workspace for monitoring and retention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8c0f8ea5cbe84839aac1d60b8bbdaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Replication">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Geo-replication is a feature of Azure Container Registry that replicates registries to multiple regions, providing resiliency against regional outages and reducing latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoscale">
  <data key="d0">Autoscale</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoscale ensures adequate resources are available by scaling out when any rule is met and scaling in when all rules are met.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale automatically adjusts throughput between a maximum value and 10% of that maximum based on application load, protecting against throttling errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale can be configured through runbook automation to ensure elasticity in response to changing traffic patterns for Azure Database for MySQL/PostgreSQL.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoscale is a scaling method that automatically adjusts resources based on demand, with settings that can scale down aggressively to reduce costs but may cause issues with sudden demand spikes or flapping.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Per-App Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Per-App Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Per-app scaling allows an application to scale independently from the App Service plan that hosts it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Service Plan">
  <data key="d0">App Service Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An App Service plan defines the compute resources for App Service, with a default soft limit of instances and support for multiple scale units and availability zone configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Storage">
  <data key="d0">Azure Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Storage is a cloud storage service offered by Microsoft Azure that serves multiple purposes across data management, diagnostics, analytics, and backup scenarios.

Azure Storage functions as a destination for ingesting both application-level and platform-level diagnostic logs. It is also used for "cold" operations data storage for analytical purposes and can serve as a target for custom backup implementations.

As a cloud storage service, Azure Storage can be configured as a linked service and data source for Azure Synapse. It also serves as an export destination for Log Analytics workspace data, supporting various redundancy levels including Zone-Redundant Storage (ZRS) and Geo-Redundant Storage (GRS). In its GRS configuration, Azure Storage is recommended for long-term operational data storage exported from Log Analytics and can also host custom visuals and plugins for Grafana.

Azure Storage Accounts are used to store operational data, exported Log Analytics data, and prepared machine learning training data.&lt;SEP&gt;An Azure service that supports zone-redundant deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Storage provides redundancy options for implementing solutions across multiple availability zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b5329d8449298032d7c7a42ce86fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active/Passive Model">
  <data key="d0">Active/Passive Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The active/passive deployment model is a multi-region strategy suitable for certain scenarios with lower reliability targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Pairs">
  <data key="d0">Regional Pairs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure regional pairs consist of two regions in a single geography, used to ensure business continuity and protection against data loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Regional pairs within a single geography provide serialized rollouts for planned maintenance and regional prioritization for unplanned maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Safe Deployment Practice Framework">
  <data key="d0">Azure Safe Deployment Practice Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure SDP framework ensures code and configuration changes undergo phased rollout with health analysis for degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geo-Redundant Storage">
  <data key="d0">Geo-Redundant Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replicates data to a secondary paired region automatically, ensuring data durability if the primary region is not recoverable.&lt;SEP&gt;GRS is the default storage for periodic backups, replicated to a paired region.&lt;SEP&gt;Geo-redundant storage (GRS) is an Azure Storage feature that replicates data using paired regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compute Decision Tree">
  <data key="d0">Compute Decision Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Compute decision tree is an Azure architecture guide for selecting appropriate compute services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3137621891148d2c190c438f188b4eb5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
