<node id="SNAT Port Exhaustion">
  <data key="d0">SNAT Port Exhaustion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SNAT port exhaustion is a common failure scenario in App Service involving outbound connections to public IP addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion occurs when a large number of outbound requests depletes available source NAT ports, preventing new outbound connections.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion is a reliability event that can occur on an egress firewall when security tooling limitations are not accounted for.&lt;SEP&gt;SNAT port exhaustion occurs when a large number of outbound requests depletes available source NAT ports, preventing new outbound connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Planned Maintenance">
  <data key="d0">Planned Maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Planned Maintenance allows defining maintenance windows for AKS cluster and node update operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calico">
  <data key="d0">Calico</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calico is a network policy option enabled through Azure CNI for controlling traffic within AKS clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;A network policy plugin for AKS with a richer feature set including support for Windows nodes and both Azure CNI and Kubenet.&lt;SEP&gt;Calico is a network policy implementation prioritized for its richer feature set and broader community support.&lt;SEP&gt;A network policy plugin for AKS with a richer feature set including support for Windows nodes and both Azure CNI and Kubenet.&lt;SEP&gt;Calico is a network policy implementation prioritized for its richer feature set and broader community support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5321cfe4fbc08d735ac5eac02e84e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kubernetes">
  <data key="d0">Kubernetes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Kubernetes is the container orchestration platform that AKS is built upon, with regular version releases.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform that includes the Network Policy feature for defining traffic rules between pods.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform where secrets can be injected as environment variables into deployments or Kubernetes secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform that includes the Network Policy feature for defining traffic rules between pods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7e299b337a793955172863127084bd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5321cfe4fbc08d735ac5eac02e84e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Kubernetes Service">
  <data key="d0">Azure Kubernetes Service</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a managed Kubernetes service on Microsoft Azure that enables quick cluster provisioning with advanced networking, identity, and reliability features. It serves as an application hosting and container orchestration platform, commonly used in baseline mission-critical architectures.

AKS supports a range of capabilities including network policies, node pools, multiple networking models, separate pod deployments on each node with updatable service definitions, and zone-redundant deployments. As an Azure PaaS product, it offers multi-region best practices and backup capabilities. AKS requires regular Kubernetes version updates and is referenced as an example for blue-green deployment architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;AKS is a managed Kubernetes service that supports network policies, node pools, and multiple networking models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1c97b53f9c2bcaf2eaf8ee6eff46b6b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c</data>
