</node>
<node id="Microsoft Defender For Container Registries">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Defender For Container Registries</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Defender for container registries provides vulnerability scanning for container images.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Containerization">
  <data key="d0">Containerization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Containerization is an abstraction layer for application code and dependencies, enabling portability and consistent execution across platforms.&lt;SEP&gt;Containerization is the strongly recommended approach for packaging and deploying mission-critical application workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite SLO">
  <data key="d0">Composite SLO</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite SLO is a reliability metric calculated across user flows, with targets of 99.99% or greater requiring a minimum of three deployment regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Composite SLO is the overall uptime objective of a solution derived from architectural decisions and individual service SLAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Content Delivery Network">
  <data key="d0">Content Delivery Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Content Delivery Network (CDN) is a distributed system that serves static content from edge nodes located closer to end users, minimizing network latency for distributed user bases. CDNs are used to offload data and improve performance, and can be incorporated as part of cost-optimization cloud patterns. However, using a CDN increases the workload surface area.

In many use cases, Azure Front Door's built-in cache can replace or eliminate the need for a dedicated CDN, as it provides similar edge caching capabilities for serving static content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Stamps">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Stamps</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment stamps are regional scale units that can be deployed across multiple regions to maximize reliability and mitigate risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment Stamps are repeatable, self-contained units that include all resources required to deliver a workload, representing workload-level redundancy with isolated failure domains and horizontal scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment Stamps is a design pattern that can be used as a variation of blue-green deployment by deploying one stamp at a time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Point Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Point Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RPO defines the acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a disaster recovery scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;RPO is configurable via consistency levels in Azure Cosmos DB, with an RPO of 0 achievable for strong consistency with single-write region.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery point objectives (RPO) are recovery targets that define the acceptable amount of data loss measured in time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RTO defines the acceptable downtime duration during a disaster recovery scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;RTO for Azure Cosmos DB regional failover is approximately 10-15 minutes, with a strategic direction to reduce to ~5 minutes via partition level failovers.&lt;SEP&gt;Recovery time objectives (RTO) are recovery targets that define how quickly a workload must be restored after a disruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linux-Based Container Runtimes">
  <data key="d0">Linux-Based Container Runtimes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Linux-based container runtimes are recommended for containers due to lightweight images and frequent feature releases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77437de30be507969c1117574fed4849</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-application-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Baseline Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The baseline architecture is a reference for mission-critical workloads accessed over public endpoints without private network connectivity requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline With Network Controls">
  <data key="d0">Baseline With Network Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An extension of the baseline architecture providing strict network controls to prevent unauthorized public access to workload resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baseline In Azure Landing Zones">
  <data key="d0">Baseline In Azure Landing Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture for deploying mission-critical workloads in enterprise setups requiring integration with centralized shared services and on-premises connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Landing Zones">
  <data key="d0">Azure Landing Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure landing zones provide a subscription model for enterprise deployments that inherits from the Corp. management group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9594ebe8dcfee62791f577e9716caf2a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core Architecture Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Core Architecture Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The core architecture pattern is a design approach for mission-critical applications consisting of global resources, regional stamp resources, and regional resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Resources">
  <data key="d0">Global Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global resources are long-living, globally shared resources that distribute traffic, store geo-replicated state, and should be configured with high availability and disaster recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Stamp Resources">
  <data key="d0">Regional Stamp Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional stamp resources are ephemeral, stateless resources deployed within a stamp that participate in completing business transactions and can be added or removed dynamically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Resources">
  <data key="d0">Regional Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional resources are deployed in a region, outlive stamp resources, and share the lifetime of the region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="North Star Design Approach">
  <data key="d0">North Star Design Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The north star design approach is a recommended design methodology for mission-critical architectures on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b2f79e880d3ae7cbc10150a4958b75f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-architecture-pattern.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979437</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Architected Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Well-Architected Assessment is a review tool for self-assessing the readiness of mission-critical workloads in production, organized to check alignment to best practices for resiliency, reliability, and availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4a64c702a6434c451dbfa718bffaf8e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission-Critical Design Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Mission-Critical Design Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mission-critical design methodology provides foundational design principles for checking design choices of a workload's architecture and end-to-end operational approach.&lt;SEP&gt;A design methodology underpinned by five key design principles that serve as a compass for design decisions across critical design areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4a64c702a6434c451dbfa718bffaf8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-assessment.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Four Vs Of Big Data">
  <data key="d0">Four Vs Of Big Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Four Vs of Big Data is a framework comprising Volume, Velocity, Variety, and Veracity used to understand characteristics for designing highly available data platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CQRS">
  <data key="d0">CQRS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is a pattern used to optimize throughput in data platforms.&lt;SEP&gt;CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) is an architectural pattern for asynchronous non-blocking messaging to load-level throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Command and Query Responsibility Segregation is a pattern for load-leveling through asynchronous non-blocking messaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Sourcing">
  <data key="d0">Event Sourcing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Sourcing is a persistence pattern used alongside CQRS to optimize data platform throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is an architectural pattern used for asynchronous non-blocking messaging.&lt;SEP&gt;Event Sourcing is a pattern used alongside CQRS for asynchronous updates to Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979578</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time To Live">
  <data key="d0">Time To Live</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time to Live (TTL) is a feature that manages data growth by automatically deleting records after an elapsed time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Mission-Critical Workload">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Mission-Critical Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Well-Architected mission-critical workload is a series of guidance articles for designing mission-critical systems on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;A series of articles providing guidance on designing and operating mission-critical workloads on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Well-Architected mission-critical workload is an article series providing design guidance for mission-critical applications on Azure.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Well-Architected mission-critical workload is an article series providing design guidance for mission-critical applications on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Write Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Write Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region write configuration enables geographically distributed writes but introduces data consistency and conflict resolution challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-region write configuration places a write replica in each deployment region to reduce latency and provide maximum redundancy at significant cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Geographical Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Geographical Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-active geographical distribution is a design recommendation that introduces challenges around data consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Volume">
  <data key="d0">Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume refers to the amount of data coming in, informing storage capacity and tiering requirements, representing the size of the dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Volume is a design consideration factor concerning data growth rates, capacity requirements, and data platform limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979579</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Velocity">
  <data key="d0">Velocity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Velocity refers to the speed at which data is processed, either as batches or continuous streams, representing the rate of flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variety">
  <data key="d0">Variety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variety refers to the organization and format of data, capturing structured, semi-structured, and unstructured formats across multiple stores or types.&lt;SEP&gt;Variety is a design consideration factor addressing data models, data types, data relationships, and query models that affect data platform decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Veracity">
  <data key="d0">Veracity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Veracity includes the provenance and curation of data sets for governance and data quality assurance, representing the accuracy of the data.&lt;SEP&gt;Veracity is a design consideration factor for validating data accuracy, encompassing consistency, security, governance, and change management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ACID">
  <data key="d0">ACID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ACID refers to full transactional semantics and traditional locking behavior, which involves trade-offs with consistency and performance in distributed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-13da8c10e8b6b19647675081cbb79073</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979580</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB SDK">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB SDK</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Cosmos DB SDK provides built-in error handling, retry, and reliability capabilities for client applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Connection Mode">
  <data key="d0">Direct Connection Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct connection mode optimizes network performance through direct TCP connectivity to backend Azure Cosmos DB nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partitioning Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Partitioning Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A partitioning strategy optimizes data distribution across logical and physical partitions according to the data model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Security Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Azure Security Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Security Baseline provides control guidance for Azure Cosmos DB Backup and Recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indexing">
  <data key="d0">Indexing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Indexing in Azure Cosmos DB is crucial for performance, using index exclusions to reduce RU/s and storage requirements by only indexing fields needed for query filtering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partition Key">
  <data key="d0">Partition Key</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A partition key is an immutable property value with high cardinality that spreads RU consumption and data storage evenly across logical and physical partitions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Backups">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Backups</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous backups provide fine granularity recovery points across the last 30 days for Azure Cosmos DB accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Failover">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Failover</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automatic failover can be configured for single write region deployments based on a defined failover priority considering all read region replicas.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic failover is strongly recommended for single write region Azure Cosmos DB deployments to handle write region outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db1b2af74d4d806b70803e4d1daf8a47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Application Architecture Guide">
  <data key="d0">Azure Application Architecture Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Application Architecture Guide provides additional data-platform guidance including decision trees and criteria for choosing data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Write">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Write</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region write is a data platform design pattern where changes to separate writeable replicas are synchronized and merged between all replicas with conflict resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Last Write Wins">
  <data key="d0">Last Write Wins</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Last Write Wins (LWW) is a conflict resolution policy that uses a time-synchronization clock protocol with a system-defined timestamp property to resolve update conflicts.&lt;SEP&gt;Last Write Wins (LWW) is the default conflict resolution policy in Azure Cosmos DB that uses a time-synchronization clock protocol to resolve conflicts by selecting the item with the highest timestamp value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paxos">
  <data key="d0">Paxos</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Paxos is a consensus protocol applied by Azure Cosmos DB to achieve quorum across replicas within a region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability Zone Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Availability Zone Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability Zone redundancy ensures data replicas are placed across multiple availability zones to protect against zone failures within a region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Connectivity Mode">
  <data key="d0">Direct Connectivity Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct mode facilitates connectivity over TCP to backend Azure Cosmos DB replica nodes for improved performance with fewer network hops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gateway Connectivity Mode">
  <data key="d0">Gateway Connectivity Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gateway mode provides HTTPS connectivity to frontend gateway nodes in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979585</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB For NoSQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB For NoSQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is the first-party API providing the richest feature set, typically receiving new capabilities first.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL is an API variant that supports custom numerical properties for conflict resolution and custom resolution policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chaos Testing">
  <data key="d0">Chaos Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chaos testing is used to test and validate backup, restore capabilities, and failover operations within continuous delivery processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing method that injects faults into an application under load to understand how it responds to failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing injects artificial failures into the system to evaluate how it reacts and validate the effectiveness of resiliency measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Chaos testing is used alongside load testing within CI/CD processes to observe and validate application health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979829</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service-Managed Encryption Keys">
  <data key="d0">Service-Managed Encryption Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service-managed encryption keys are recommended to reduce management complexity when applying encryption to data platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer-Managed Keys">
  <data key="d0">Customer-Managed Keys</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer-managed keys are encryption keys managed by the customer, requiring appropriate key management procedures for availability, backup, and rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Data Services">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Data Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized data services (Central IT DBaaS) introduce operational bottlenecks that hinder agility and should be avoided in mission-critical or business-critical contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cassandra">
  <data key="d0">Cassandra</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cassandra is one of the API options supported by Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MongoDB">
  <data key="d0">MongoDB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MongoDB is one of the API options supported by Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd60f6e9fffcac30f5165dbde144c70b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Request Units">
  <data key="d0">Request Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Request Units per second (RU/s) are the measure of throughput provisioned in Azure Cosmos DB, billed per region.&lt;SEP&gt;Request Units (RUs) are the billing unit for Azure Cosmos DB, charged per region when replicated across multiple regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Feed">
  <data key="d0">Change Feed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Azure Cosmos DB change feed provides a time-ordered feed of insert and update operations to data in a container, excluding deletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB change feed writes data to separate storage and supports continuous or periodic custom backups but does not yet reflect deletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Change feed is a mechanism in Azure Cosmos DB that captures data record changes for propagation to target data stores.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Locks">
  <data key="d0">Resource Locks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resource Locks protect Azure Cosmos DB resources against incorrect modification or deletion, applying only to control plane operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Resource locks are an Azure feature to prevent resources from being modified or deleted, recommended mainly for long-lived global resources rather than ephemeral regional resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980011</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soft Delete">
  <data key="d0">Soft Delete</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Soft Delete is a pattern where data records are flagged as deleted rather than explicitly removed, enabling inclusion in the change feed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session">
  <data key="d0">Session</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Session is the default and most widely used consistency level in Azure Cosmos DB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosmos DB Account Reader">
  <data key="d0">Cosmos DB Account Reader</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A built-in RBAC role that enables read-only access to Azure Cosmos DB resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DocumentDB Account Contributor">
  <data key="d0">DocumentDB Account Contributor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A built-in RBAC role that enables management of Azure Cosmos DB accounts including keys and role assignments but not data-plane access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosmos DB Operator">
  <data key="d0">Cosmos DB Operator</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A built-in RBAC role similar to DocumentDB Account Contributor but without ability to manage keys or role assignments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0709e0d30d586072a6b10881d6bc306c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Database For PostgreSQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure Database For PostgreSQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Database For PostgreSQL is a managed relational database offered in Single Server, Flexible Server, and Hyperscale (Citus) deployment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Database for PostgreSQL is a managed database service on Azure offering Single Server, Flexible Server, and Hyperscale (Citus) deployment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Database For PostgreSQL is a managed database service offering Flexible Server and Hyperscale (Citus) options for business critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Database for PostgreSQL supports point-in-time restore with backup and restore capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cache For Redis">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cache For Redis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cache for Redis is an in-memory caching service based on open source Redis, offering Premium, Enterprise, and Enterprise Flash tiers with geo-replication and high availability capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse is an enterprise analytical platform combining relational and non-relational data with Spark technologies and built-in Azure service integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse brings together analytics capabilities including SQL data warehousing, Spark big data, and Data Explorer for log and time series analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse is an enterprise analytical platform that brings together relational and non-relational data with Spark technologies, including SQL data warehousing, Spark big data, and Data Explorer for log and time series analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Analytics is an analytical technology offering ML capabilities, Spark Pools, notebooks, and data integration for building AIOps models.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse is used for analysis of ingested Log Analytics operational data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperscale (Citus)">
  <data key="d0">Hyperscale (Citus)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperscale (Citus) is a PostgreSQL deployment option providing dynamic scalability through sharding, with 99.95% SLA when High Availability is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperscale (Citus) is a deployment option for Azure Database for PostgreSQL that provides dynamic scalability through sharding, with SLA 99.95% when High Availability is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperscale (Citus) is a configuration option for Azure Database For PostgreSQL that maximizes availability across multiple nodes with High Availability mode offering 99.95% SLA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Server">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Server</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexible Server is a deployment option offering Availability Zone redundancy with SLA 99.99%, cost efficiencies through stop/start capability, and burstable compute tier.&lt;SEP&gt;Flexible Server is a deployment option for Azure Database For PostgreSQL recommended for business critical workloads due to Availability Zone support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enterprise Flash Tier">
  <data key="d0">Enterprise Flash Tier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enterprise Flash tier of Azure Cache for Redis uses RAM and flash non-volatile memory, enabling cache sizes up to 13TB with clustering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point-In-Time Restore">
  <data key="d0">Point-In-Time Restore</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Point-in-time restore (PITR) allows restoring data to a specific moment with one-second granularity within the continuous backup window.&lt;SEP&gt;Point-in-time restore is an operational playbook method to recover from severe configuration errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Point-in-time restore is an operational recovery method for Azure SQL Database to recover from severe configuration errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching For Hot Tier Data">
  <data key="d0">Caching For Hot Tier Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An in-memory caching layer that enhances data platforms by increasing read throughput and improving response times for hot tier data scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytical Scenarios">
  <data key="d0">Analytical Scenarios</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytical scenarios drive additional value from data flows in mission-critical applications, requiring different data platform capabilities than transactional workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-058624a53f7dcacddad189523984d8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAGA">
  <data key="d0">SAGA</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SAGA is a design pattern applied to manage consistency and dependencies between different datastores.&lt;SEP&gt;SAGA is a design pattern used where dependencies between datastores exist in microservice architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-To-Live">
  <data key="d0">Time-To-Live</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time-To-Live (TTL) is a data expiration mechanism for removing data no longer required.&lt;SEP&gt;Time-To-Live (TTL) is a setting that enables Azure Cosmos DB to automatically delete expired data, used with the soft-delete pattern to ensure deletions propagate through the change feed before removal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Tiering">
  <data key="d0">Data Tiering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data tiering classifies datasets into 'hot', 'warm', and 'cold' tiers based on usage and criticality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacity Model">
  <data key="d0">Capacity Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A capacity model monitors data volume against scale limits and expected growth rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A model enabling planning of resource scale levels for a given load profile and system-wide capacity allocation planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft is the company that provides the Azure cloud platform, offering a wide range of services including Azure-native toolsets for deploying and managing mission-critical applications. Microsoft is responsible for Azure platform services, future platform investments, and manages core infrastructure such as the backbone network, Azure IP Ranges, and Service Tags.

Microsoft manages Azure infrastructure encompassing data synchronization, traffic distribution, and failover capabilities. The company is responsible for automatic failover during availability zone outages in zone-redundant deployments and handles remediation of service outages, including DDoS L3 and L4 protection.

Microsoft also provides the Zero Trust security model and Microsoft Entra identity services. Additionally, Microsoft offers discounted rates for predictable long-term commitments to specific resources or resource categories.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft operates the backbone network and manages Azure IP Ranges and Service Tags.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983280</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservice Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Microservice Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A microservice architecture allows individual application services to be built with distinct scenario-optimized datastores.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservice architecture is a design principle promoting loosely coupled services that can use distinct data stores and scenario-optimized data technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Data Platform">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Data Platform</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A multi-region data platform distributes replicas across regions for maximum reliability, availability, and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching">
  <data key="d0">Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Caching is used for 'hot' data scenarios to minimize response times, with policies for expiration and housekeeping.&lt;SEP&gt;Caching of static content at the edge speeds up client load times, reduces backend load, and lowers costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Caching is a design component that can optimize system performance and improve user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Caching of static content at the edge speeds up client load times, reduces backend load, and lowers costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32d784320f22fc18cf5d44108f55403f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching Layer">
  <data key="d0">Caching Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A caching layer is used to increase read throughput and improve user experience and end-to-end client response times.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Model">
  <data key="d0">Data Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The data model, along with data types and relationships, strongly affects data platform decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CAP Theorem">
  <data key="d0">CAP Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The CAP theorem expresses the trade-off between consistency and latency in distributed applications with multiple data replicas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PACELC Theorem">
  <data key="d0">PACELC Theorem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The PACELC theorem extends CAP to express trade-offs between consistency, availability, and latency in distributed systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apache Spark">
  <data key="d0">Apache Spark</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Apache Spark is an analytical runtime environment that may have integration restrictions for analyzing polyglot data structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key Vault">
  <data key="d0">Key Vault</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Key Vault is a secure location for managing encryption keys, used with both client-side and server-side encryption.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Vault is an Azure secret management solution that supports zone and regional redundancy and integrates with Microsoft Entra ID.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Vault is a global managed service that implements redundancy transparently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MACsec">
  <data key="d0">MACsec</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MACsec (IEEE 802.1AE MAC) is a data-link encryption method used to secure all traffic between Azure datacenters on the Microsoft backbone network.&lt;SEP&gt;MACsec is data-link layer encryption used on underlying network hardware to secure data in-transit between Azure data centers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Backbone Network">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Backbone Network</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft backbone network carries traffic between Azure datacenters, secured by MACsec encryption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyglot Storage">
  <data key="d0">Polyglot Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyglot storage refers to the capability of analytical datastores to support various types of data structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client-Side Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-side encryption is an encryption method implemented in the application layer where keys can be managed in Key Vault or another secure location.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Server-Side Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Server-Side Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Server-side encryption is an encryption method implemented in the data layer using service-managed or customer-managed keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conflict Resolution">
  <data key="d0">Conflict Resolution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conflict resolution addresses situations in multi-region write contexts where the same data item is changed in separate write-replicas, using policies such as Last Write Wins or custom strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ceea393f341ad536e3a85d5af262a1bf</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Resolution Policies">
  <data key="d0">Custom Resolution Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Custom resolution policies allow application-defined semantics to reconcile conflicts using a registered merge stored procedure, available only with Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paxos Consensus Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Paxos Consensus Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Paxos consensus protocol is applied within the hub region to achieve quorum across replicas for conflict resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hub Region">
  <data key="d0">Hub Region</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hub region is the primary single region in Azure Cosmos DB's multi-region write configuration responsible for performing all conflict resolutions, determined by the first region configured.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Buffer">
  <data key="d0">Message Buffer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The message buffer stores write conflicts within the hub region to load level and provide redundancy for transient faults, capable of storing a few minutes worth of write updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Levels">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistency levels in Azure Cosmos DB configure RPO and RTO trade-offs between data durability and throughput, with five levels available including strong and relaxed options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab7e9f04e877c8420f5dae1ad6375e0f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Link">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse Link provides an analytical store whose data is not included in Azure Cosmos DB backups.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link connects Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store to Azure Synapse for performing analytics on operational data without impacting transactional performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Synapse Link enables direct querying of Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store from Azure Synapse, enabling no-ETL Hybrid Transactional-Analytical Processing (HTAP).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Data Factory">
  <data key="d0">Azure Data Factory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Data Factory (ADF) is a batch-oriented orchestration service that supports copying data from Azure Cosmos DB with various trigger types and Azure Private Link support.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Data Factory provides ETL tools that natively integrate with Azure Synapse for data extraction, transformation, and loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Private Link">
  <data key="d0">Azure Private Link</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Private Link is supported by Azure Data Factory for high network security scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Private Link provides dedicated access to Azure PaaS resources using private IP addresses and private network connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB For Nosql">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB For Nosql</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL offers the most comprehensive feature set, particularly for performance tuning.&lt;SEP&gt;An Azure Cosmos DB API that supports continuous backup configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Feed Processor">
  <data key="d0">Change Feed Processor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The change feed processor is a component that binds to the Azure Cosmos DB change feed to process items into storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soft-Delete Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Soft-Delete Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A pattern where data records are updated with a deleted flag instead of being explicitly deleted, combined with TTL for automatic cleanup after change feed propagation.&lt;SEP&gt;A soft-delete pattern using a boolean property and TTL must be applied with the change feed since it does not yet reflect deletes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caad63f908cd3b639ca5d51c5a2341ae</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Event Grid">
  <data key="d0">Azure Event Grid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Event Grid is supported by Azure Data Factory as a trigger mechanism for backup pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single-Region Write Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Single-Region Write Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Single-region write configuration with globally distributed read replicas offers high reliability at a more compelling price-point with 99.999% read and 99.995% write SLAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd806d5f85dca98a80362955d10e7ef7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure SQL Database">
  <data key="d0">Azure SQL Database</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SQL Database is a fully managed relational database engine providing high availability, geo-replication, auto failover groups, and up to 99.995% SLA.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL Database is a mature relational database service on Azure with wide reliability capabilities, recommended for relational requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL Database is an Azure PaaS product with disaster recovery guidance and backup recovery capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL Database is a relational database service supporting readable replicas and automatic failover group capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL Database supports point-in-time restore functionality for rollback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9314d7889b0915883928ca0b8ed3e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Failover Groups">
  <data key="d0">Auto Failover Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Failover Groups replicate databases to a secondary server and allow transparent failover in case of failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Failover Groups provide transparent failover to a secondary region with geo-replication for read optimization and database redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharding">
  <data key="d0">Sharding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sharding distributes data and processing across multiple identical structured databases by partitioning horizontally.&lt;SEP&gt;Sharding is a method to partition relational databases based on different application and data contexts to maximize scalability, availability, and fault isolation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store applies a column format for optimized analytical queries with multi-region availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store is an optimized column store for analytical queries on Azure Cosmos DB operational data.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cosmos DB Analytical Store is a schematized, fully isolated column-oriented data store that enables large-scale analytics on Azure Cosmos DB data without impacting transactional workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Traffic Manager">
  <data key="d0">Azure Traffic Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Traffic Manager is a globally distributed DNS-based routing service provided by Microsoft Azure. It operates as a DNS redirection service, routing traffic based on configured rules without processing request payloads, leveraging DNS TTL caching for efficiency. It is not deployed into a specific region but functions as a global load balancer with built-in multi-region redundancy and availability, and can be configured across multiple regions for added resilience.

Azure Traffic Manager serves as a global routing service particularly suited for non-HTTP/S scenarios, acting as an alternative to Azure Front Door. In the context of Azure SQL Database, it controls routing to specific gateway rings. Its DNS-level operation means it directs clients to appropriate endpoints without handling the actual data traffic itself.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc30613029b54ffcf46bef5325576b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b609a802fa10d995d38905fc231483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cosmos DB Change Feed">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cosmos DB Change Feed</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cosmos DB change feed can maintain a separate secondary data store for analytical scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Cosmos DB change feed can be used to maintain a separate secondary data store for analytical scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Synapse Studio">
  <data key="d0">Azure Synapse Studio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Synapse Studio unites ingestion and querying tasks for analytical use cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-267380e50f87e200b9b8528082b05e30</data>
