  <data key="d5">1776979594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL">
  <data key="d0">ETL</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Extract, Transform, and Load (ETL) pipelines are used to extract data into separate data platforms for analytical queries, consuming throughput and impacting transactional workload performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Extract, Transform, Load (ETL) is a traditional data processing approach that may not scale with deployment telemetry growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979679</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-Sync">
  <data key="d0">Auto-Sync</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto-Sync is the process where operational data changes are automatically synced to the Analytical Store, usually with latency less than two minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-111b4be7044ec226f9516d7ed5776826</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
