  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant Deployment Model">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant Deployment Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Zone-Redundant deployment model spreads Business Critical database replicas within the same region across Availability Zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserved Capacity">
  <data key="d0">Reserved Capacity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserved Capacity provides potential cost optimizations for Azure SQL Database and Azure Database for PostgreSQL compute costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65d6d67b4e65531ad950d1206265e623</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-data-platform.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penetration Testing">
  <data key="d0">Penetration Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Penetration testing ensures that an application and its environment meet the requirements of an expected security posture by identifying security vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Penetration testing ensures that an application and its environment meet security posture requirements by identifying security vulnerabilities, including end-to-end software supply chain and package dependency scanning for known CVEs.&lt;SEP&gt;Penetration testing simulates real-world attacks to validate security defenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Penetration testing is performed by third-party security practitioners to assess system security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Vulnerabilities And Exposures">
  <data key="d0">Common Vulnerabilities And Exposures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) is a system for identifying known security vulnerabilities that are scanned and monitored in software supply chains.&lt;SEP&gt;CVEs are tracked within utilized package dependencies as part of securing the software supply chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Chaos Studio">
  <data key="d0">Azure Chaos Studio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Chaos Studio is a native suite of chaos experimentation tools that enables conducting chaos experiments and injecting faults within Azure services and application components.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Chaos Studio is a managed service that uses chaos engineering to measure, understand, and improve cloud application resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrastructure As Code">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure As Code</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is a practice that treats infrastructure definitions as version-controlled source code, using declarative artifacts such as Terraform, ARM templates, or Bicep to automate the provisioning and management of resources, particularly in environments like Azure. IaC defines the desired state of all infrastructure, promoting consistency across environments, eliminating human error, and providing traceability, rollback capabilities, and self-documentation.

IaC is recommended as the preferred approach for infrastructure changes, supporting safe deployment practices through automation and consistency. It favors declarative methods over imperative ones as a standardized approach to preparing resources and configurations.

However, IaC is not without risks. Highly layered, modularized, or heavily parameterized designs can increase the chance of accidental misconfiguration, requiring careful design and governance to maintain the reliability benefits IaC is intended to provide.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure as code (IaC) is recommended for consistent, version-controlled management of health models.&lt;SEP&gt;An approach to building solutions that enables quick redeployment into another region during a major disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;An approach (IaC) for building solutions that enables quick redeployment into another region during a disaster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeefe2d63573562646e740d09fa6d491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a688a846e77a6107a53c8f43220265c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d847dca2d14a4e01f2ac8a1fb0f3723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GitHub Actions">
  <data key="d0">GitHub Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GitHub Actions is an Azure-native toolset for deploying and managing mission-critical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;GitHub Actions is an Azure-native toolset suited for build tasks (continuous integration).&lt;SEP&gt;GitHub Actions is a tool for deployment targeting different environments, documented by GitHub.&lt;SEP&gt;GitHub Actions supports multi-stage deployments using approval gates for progressive exposure rollout.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e44080944c7ed0bdb8917734103e726b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Pipelines">
  <data key="d0">Azure Pipelines</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Pipelines is an Azure-native toolset for deploying and managing mission-critical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Pipelines is an Azure-native toolset recommended for mission-critical deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Pipelines supports multi-stage deployments using approval gates for progressive exposure rollout.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c97a1db66c7ecde12774487f7afb1593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ecbdde6d262012ebbdfa789102231a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8</data>
