  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Framework Mission-Critical Workload">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Framework Mission-Critical Workload</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A series of articles providing guidance on designing mission-critical workloads on Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terraform">
  <data key="d0">Terraform</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Terraform is an infrastructure as code tool used for managing deployment environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Terraform is an infrastructure-as-code tool whose resources can be used for common design patterns alongside Azure policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Terraform is an infrastructure-as-code solution for automating provisioning of Azure resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dfe7557b9ff125211f2a2e03cb3dce</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Resource Manager Templates">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Manager Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ARM templates are infrastructure as code artifacts used for deploying Azure resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Development Environment">
  <data key="d0">Development Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Development environments are short-lived environments with lower reliability and security requirements, created for parallel feature development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Or Staging Environment">
  <data key="d0">Test Or Staging Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Test or staging environments are short-lived environments used for validation that should reflect production for reliability, capacity, and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Validation And Testing">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Validation And Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous validation and testing describes appropriate test cycles performed to ensure bug-free deployment to production for mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A section describing appropriate tests for mission-critical workloads, emphasizing rigorous and ongoing testing practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous validation and testing is a critical activity for validating application code and infrastructure health across reliability, performance, availability, security, quality, and scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Automated testing within CI/CD processes including load testing and chaos experimentation to validate thresholds and identify risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06f6956528b19bfc513c2a4b70a66e71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue/Green Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Blue/Green Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model requiring at least two identical deployments where traffic is gradually transitioned from the active (blue) to the new (green) deployment, enabling zero-downtime upgrades.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue/green deployment is a strategy that uses transient resource duplication to mitigate reliability impact during deployments, increasing costs during those periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue/green deployment is a deployment model used in operational excellence practices.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment model that introduces side-by-side deployments on production platforms, requiring preemptive scaling or dormant deployments for rollback support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c68f04b50833c59213a11d31e461972</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staging Environment">
  <data key="d0">Staging Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Short-lived environments that reflect production for testing and validation, destroyed after test validations are complete.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Production Environment">
  <data key="d0">Production Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environments requiring the highest levels of reliability, capacity, and security, with special data management needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Front Door">
  <data key="d0">Azure Front Door</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Front Door is a globally distributed Azure service that provides HTTP/S load balancing, traffic routing, content delivery, and traffic acceleration across multiple regions. It leverages Anycast protocol connectivity to route user requests to the nearest edge location, improving latency for geographically dispersed users. As a global Azure resource, it is not deployed into a specific region.

Azure Front Door offers built-in edge caching for both static and dynamic content, Web Application Firewall (WAF) integration for protecting global HTTP/S applications, TLS/SSL certificate management and renewal, health probes, session affinity, load distribution, and DDoS protection. Its service tags can be used in Network Security Groups (NSGs) to validate legitimate backend traffic.

Azure Front Door supports replica-aware, priority-based global routing and can orchestrate automated traffic transitions between environments, such as blue-green deployments. Its request count serves as a key metric for operational dashboards and monitoring. In practice, it is used as a front-end for applications such as the e-commerce website in the FMA example, delivering and protecting global HTTP/S applications spanning multiple Azure regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is a globally distributed service providing HTTP/S load balancing, Anycast protocol connectivity, built-in caching, WAF support, and multi-region redundancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is a global traffic routing service for HTTP/S scenarios that provides edge caching, WAF integration, health probes, load distribution, session affinity, TLS certificate management, and DDoS protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is a global load balancer and routing service that provides WAF, TLS management, edge caching, and health probing capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is a global Azure resource that accepts HTTP/HTTPS traffic, provides WAF capabilities, managed certificates, and DDoS protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Front Door is an Azure service providing global routing, WAF capabilities, and edge caching for static and dynamic content delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;A service used for routing traffic, with service tags used in NSGs to validate legitimate backend traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Mission-Critical">
  <data key="d0">Azure Mission-Critical</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An approach recommending blue/green deployment where infrastructure and applications are deployed together as part of a deployment stamp.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Load Generator">
  <data key="d0">User Load Generator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tool provided in the Mission Critical Online reference implementation for generating synthetic user load for realistic testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c437470f34ed638659632da76be560f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue-Green Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Blue-Green Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue-green deployment is a deployment strategy where traffic is transitioned between two environments (blue and green), with the inactive environment decommissioned after transition.&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment uses two identical infrastructure pools, routing traffic gradually from the current version (blue) to the updated version (green).&lt;SEP&gt;Blue-green deployment is a deployment model that swaps between two environments to minimize downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit Testing">
  <data key="d0">Unit Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Unit testing confirms that application business logic works as expected and validates the overall effect of code changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smoke Testing">
  <data key="d0">Smoke Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Smoke testing identifies whether infrastructure and application components are available and function as expected, typically testing a single virtual user session.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UI Testing">
  <data key="d0">UI Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">UI testing validates that application user interfaces are deployed and that user interface interactions function as expected using automation tools.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Testing">
  <data key="d0">Performance Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance testing combines aspects of load and stress testing to validate performance under load and establish benchmark behaviors.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance testing is a key capability used to define and continually evaluate application health under steady state reflective of production load.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance testing is a method used to detect performance issues and enable measure/improve cycles for workload teams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subscription-Scoped Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Subscription-Scoped Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subscription-scoped deployment involves using multiple Azure subscriptions as scale units to avoid single subscription scale limits for mission-critical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b8200e1f0295324acfed0587523ace64</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-deployment-testing.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Level Objectives">
  <data key="d0">Service Level Objectives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Level Objectives (SLOs) define availability targets such as 99.9% vs. 99.999% availability for mission-critical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979707</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Time Objective">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Time Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Time Objective (RTO) defines the acceptable time to recover an application after failure.&lt;SEP&gt;RTO is the maximum acceptable time to restore business operations after a disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;RTO represents the target time to restore a solution to a working state after an outage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recovery Point Objective">
  <data key="d0">Recovery Point Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recovery Point Objective (RPO) defines the acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a failure.&lt;SEP&gt;RPO is the maximum acceptable amount of data loss measured in time during a disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;RPO represents the acceptable amount of data loss, controlled by backup frequency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero-Downtime Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Zero-Downtime Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zero-downtime deployments ensure users experience no disruption during changes, requiring rigorous testing and end-to-end automation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979708</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="End-To-End Automation">
  <data key="d0">End-To-End Automation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">End-to-end automation spans deployment and management activities to ensure consistency, repeatability, and resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979708</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Architected Framework">
  <data key="d0">Well-Architected Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Well-Architected Framework provides design pillars that apply to mission-critical workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;The Well-Architected Framework provides best practices as technical foundation for building reliable solutions, with pillars including Reliability, Security, Operational Excellence, and Performance Efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The Well-Architected Framework consists of five pillars that automation tooling should adhere to as part of workload design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e21bfd072e50a8d166c6a4fdcae0f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability">
  <data key="d0">Reliability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reliability is a core design pillar and workload quality pillar within the Well-Architected Framework, serving as the primary focus for mission-critical workloads. It is centered on ensuring systems are resilient, stable, and capable of surviving failures while consistently meeting defined reliability objectives, resiliency targets, and recovery goals during malfunctions or disasters.

Key principles of Reliability include maximizing availability through active/active design, fault isolation, health monitoring, automation, self-healing, and complexity avoidance. It emphasizes replication, redundancy, simplicity, and limiting the blast radius of malfunctions. The pillar prioritizes minimizing points of failure and reducing critical dependencies to ensure workloads are manageable and repeatable through proper infrastructure and application design.

Reliability involves associated tradeoffs with other pillars, requiring careful balancing of design decisions to achieve optimal system recovery and resilience against failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability is a pillar that prioritizes simplicity and avoidance of destabilizing activities in workload design.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability refers to a workload's ability to avoid and recover from malfunctions and meet service-level objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability is a pillar with its own set of tradeoffs.&lt;SEP&gt;A pillar of the Azure Well-Architected Framework focused on mitigating risks through geographically distributed workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;Reliability is a pillar concern in Azure deployment approaches, ranging from low in locally redundant to high or very high in zone-redundant and multi-region deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Performance Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance Efficiency is a design pillar focused on ensuring workloads can meet demand effectively while maintaining optimal resource utilization. It emphasizes having just enough supply to handle demand at all times, avoiding over-provisioning while still achieving performance targets. Core principles include scale-out design, automation for hyperscale, continuous validation, managed compute services, baseline performance establishment, and capacity modeling.

Performance Efficiency defines availability as a consistent level of application service and performance relative to a known healthy state. It involves distributing load across multiple redundant nodes, scaling systems up and down to adapt to changing demands, and maintaining user experience while conserving resources. Key focus areas include reducing latency and overhead, code optimizations, design patterns, capacity planning, resource segmentation, and supply-demand balance to ensure efficiency of every interaction as demand increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Efficiency is a pillar that recommends allocating as much compute and network as possible to workload requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Efficiency emphasizes meeting performance targets without spending more than necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Efficiency is a pillar that emphasizes meeting performance targets without spending more than necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;A pillar addressing network latency and communication between availability zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance Efficiency is a pillar concern that varies by deployment approach, with zonal pinned offering high performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Excellence">
  <data key="d0">Operational Excellence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operational Excellence is a design pillar focused on building reliable, repeatable, and safe operations through DevOps practices, automation, and observability. It emphasizes loosely coupled components, automated build and release processes, and standardized workflows that ensure workload quality and team cohesion.

Operational Excellence is rooted in a culture of blamelessness, respect, and continuous improvement. It requires architectures to be serviceable and observable, prioritizing simplicity and manageable operations. The pillar recommends maintaining documentation repositories for procedures and topologies. It covers key areas including development practices, observability, release management, safe deployment, configuration, failover, and maintenance practices.

Operational Excellence directly impacts application availability by addressing how a workload responds to operational issues. It establishes clear team standards around responsibility, accountability, and customer outcomes, while emphasizing SDLC rigor. The pillar serves the long-term best interests of both the workload and the team, and carries its own set of tradeoffs when balanced against other pillars. It is particularly concerned with managing the complexity of deploying and operating resources across different deployment approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeefe2d63573562646e740d09fa6d491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e44080944c7ed0bdb8917734103e726b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security">
  <data key="d0">Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security is one of the five mission-critical design principles and a workload quality pillar that addresses the protection and safety of workloads against threats intended to directly or indirectly compromise their reliability. It provides confidentiality, integrity, and availability assurances for workload systems and user data.

Security covers a broad range of areas including threat modeling, endpoint protection, code vulnerability protection, encryption, least privilege automation, access controls, logging, testing, and compliance. It prioritizes reduced surface area, active security controls, and current software patching to minimize attack vectors. Security also addresses how a workload mitigates specific threats such as DDoS attacks, with significant bearing on overall reliability, requiring controls for both software development and operational components.&lt;SEP&gt;Security is a design pillar that prioritizes defense in depth, reduced surface area, and strong segmentation to minimize attack vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Security is a pillar with associated tradeoffs.&lt;SEP&gt;Security is a pillar focused on reducing workload surface area, protecting data confidentiality, and implementing segmentation strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Security encompasses confidentiality, integrity, and availability protections for a workload.&lt;SEP&gt;Security is a pillar with its own set of tradeoffs.&lt;SEP&gt;A pillar of the Azure Well-Architected Framework that applies regardless of deployment design; Azure applies the same security rigor to every region and availability zone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e8384b0bc1068b56283b3c6b4bb02b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be68d72fe0d93ad1cb453304822afbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-overview.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Cost Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost Optimization is one of the five mission-critical design principles and a workload quality pillar focused on maximizing return on investment while minimizing waste, unnecessary expenditure, and underutilized resources. It emphasizes driving down resource demand to enable the use of cheaper SKUs, fewer instances, and reduced consumption, while also reducing component diversity and increasing density.

As a continuous practice, Cost Optimization involves right-sizing investment as workloads evolve, evaluating the value of deployed solutions, avoiding over-provisioning, and consolidating resources where possible. It prioritizes long-term financial responsibility through continuous monitoring, repeatable processes, and balancing actual costs versus perceived value. This includes reducing resource spending, tooling sprawl, and pursuing vendor consolidation.

Cost Optimization seeks to maximize the value produced by a workload's resources without exceeding performance targets, all within financial constraints. It aligns with broader governance disciplines of cost management and considers tradeoffs with other pillars, such as reliability, avoiding over-engineering beyond what business requirements demand. These associated tradeoffs must be carefully balanced against other design principles.&lt;SEP&gt;A pillar concerning resource costs, network traffic charges, and ongoing management costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost Optimization is a pillar concern varying from low cost for locally redundant deployments to high cost for multi-region deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb547f72466f2ff769350152ae4ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4024f3337155e70539ba954cfd01caab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21e41edd72b9157b512d1a210db4941b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f75cb5e98d1eaef8d795bebeeb3d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active/Active Design">
  <data key="d0">Active/Active Design</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where solution components are distributed across multiple Availability Zones and Azure regions to maximize availability and achieve regional fault tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blast Radius Reduction And Fault Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Blast Radius Reduction And Fault Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of designing solutions in a resilient manner by anticipating failures and correlated impact from individual components to entire Azure regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Self-Healing">
  <data key="d0">Design For Self-Healing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A concept describing a system's ability to deal with failures automatically through pre-defined remediation protocols connected to failure modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Scale-Out">
  <data key="d0">Design For Scale-Out</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A concept focusing on horizontal growth by adding resource units in parallel instead of increasing existing resource sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observe Application Health">
  <data key="d0">Observe Application Health</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of monitoring application operation relative to a known healthy state to detect or predict reliability issues and enable swift remedial action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drive Automation">
  <data key="d0">Drive Automation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle emphasizing automation in all aspects of a cloud solution to minimize human error and improve reliability through automated testing, deployment, and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complexity Avoidance">
  <data key="d0">Complexity Avoidance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design consideration to avoid unnecessary complexity in solution design and operational processes to drive reliability and management efficiencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loosely Coupled Components">
  <data key="d0">Loosely Coupled Components</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method enabling independent testing, deployments, and updates to application components while minimizing inter-team dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automate Build And Release Processes">
  <data key="d0">Automate Build And Release Processes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of fully automating build and release processes to reduce friction, increase deployment velocity, and bring repeatability and consistency across environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Managed Compute Services">
  <data key="d0">Managed Compute Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Using managed compute services and containerized architectures to reduce ongoing administrative and operational overhead of designing, operating, and scaling applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86c34d935d91c0feba2784fca188c36</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SIEM">
  <data key="d0">SIEM</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Information and Event Management tooling used for tracking security and audit events and incident response.&lt;SEP&gt;A SIEM is specialized observability tooling that performs aggregation and threat intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981230</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Continuity">
  <data key="d0">Business Continuity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Planning and practice drills essential for maximizing resiliency in the event of unplanned downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disaster Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Disaster Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disaster Recovery (DR) is a structured set of strategies, plans, and procedures designed to restore workloads, systems, and data after failures, outages, or significant incidents. It encompasses planning, failover, and recovery procedures aligned with defined recovery targets to maximize business resiliency.

DR often involves maintaining a preserved safe system state to fail over to a secure secondary system or location, including geo-distant environment strategies to mitigate risk from large-scale events such as geographic disasters. Planning and practice drills are conducted frequently to iteratively improve procedures.

DR solutions such as backups increase workload surface area and require additional security controls. They can also lead to excess costs if they excessively satisfy recovery objectives, making it important to balance recovery capabilities with cost and security considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery involves reliably recovering a workload from all forms of disaster, with complexity increased by security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Disaster recovery (DR) is a mitigation strategy that all workloads must have regardless of reliability targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efa918a51cded76ba3c94dc0ae8e7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-579193d2ba0036e6c770c9b7c78ebbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c93cee43dab578364cd13532355256b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9935cc9222b0d130d80a116c87875301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51316135aacca9fd878154c3dd2abcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/disaster-recovery.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DDoS">
  <data key="d0">DDoS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distributed Denial-Of-Service attacks are common attack vectors against network endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Denial-Of-Service attacks are known to have catastrophic impact on availability and performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980094</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Dashboards">
  <data key="d0">Azure Dashboards</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Dashboards provides integrated out-of-the-box visualization for operational data within Azure Monitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Dashboards is a visualization tool for representing health models and business requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979822</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grafana">
  <data key="d0">Grafana</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Grafana is a visualization tool used to represent aggregated health scores as dependency charts.&lt;SEP&gt;Grafana is a market-leading observability and visualization solution, also available as Azure Managed Grafana.&lt;SEP&gt;Grafana is an alternative visualization solution with market-leading capabilities and an extensive open-source plugin ecosystem, recommended when Azure Dashboards are insufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Grafana is an operational tool used for dashboards that can incorporate health insights.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58687539bce004e3d6c298bc58bb0198</data>
