<node id="Correlation ID">
  <data key="d0">Correlation ID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A correlation ID is an identifier returned to callers for all calls to facilitate troubleshooting and error tracking.&lt;SEP&gt;A correlation ID traverses service boundaries to track requests throughout an application and pinpoint the cause of failure across multiple services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef87f84d908a2e8bef1511aac0487905</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traffic Light Model">
  <data key="d0">Traffic Light Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The traffic light model uses Green, Amber, and Red to represent Healthy, Degraded, and Unavailable application states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
