  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ExpressRoute">
  <data key="d0">ExpressRoute</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ExpressRoute is an Azure platform resource used for on-premises communication that may be a key dependency.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute is an Azure service providing secure connections with bandwidths up to 100 Gbps.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute with private peering is used to access Azure PaaS services from on-premises in hybrid application scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute is used to access Azure PaaS services from on-premises via private peering for hybrid application scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;ExpressRoute is an Azure service providing secure connections with bandwidths up to 100 Gbps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09511819f8c1ba5a16e71983efd9f8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Action Groups">
  <data key="d0">Action Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Action Groups are Azure Monitor components used to define automated responses to alerts, with limits on configurable responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979826</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Database For Postgres">
  <data key="d0">Azure Database For Postgres</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Database for Postgres can serve as an external datastore for Grafana configuration state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979826</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="App Services">
  <data key="d0">App Services</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">App Services is a low-friction container platform used for deploying Grafana nodes in a highly available configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979826</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure SQL">
  <data key="d0">Azure SQL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure SQL is a high-performance datastore that can be used to optimize dashboard data retrieval when Log Analytics query limits are reached.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL databases are used in the e-commerce FMA example.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure SQL is a database service with features like auto-failover groups, private endpoints, and network security groups for protection.&lt;SEP&gt;An Azure service that supports zone-redundant deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a80a8926c38685348cb6badf1d2485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981733</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Incident Response">
  <data key="d0">Automated Incident Response</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated incident response is the practice of implementing extensive alerting to detect proactively and respond to issues in near real-time, maximizing reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979827</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Monitor Alerts API">
  <data key="d0">Azure Monitor Alerts API</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Monitor Alerts API is used to gather historic alerts for cold operational storage and advanced analytics.&lt;SEP&gt;The Azure Monitor Alerts API is used to retrieve active and historic alerts, with throttling limits for extreme usage scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Monitor Alerts API is used to retrieve historic alerts for operational data storage and ML model use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979827</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KQL">
  <data key="d0">KQL</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">KQL (Kusto Query Language) is used to query and aggregate health metrics from InsightsMetrics and AzureMetrics to compute health status and scores.&lt;SEP&gt;KQL (Kusto Query Language) provides operators like 'union' to aggregate queries and mitigate Log Analytics query limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a26205fb34c4e32a46218f4e0a88ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979827</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Health Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Health modeling is a process of defining a robust health model by mapping quantified application health states through observability and operational constructs to maximize reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling is an approach used to anticipate issues before they become incidents and affect customer experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling is a method used in monitoring to anticipate issues before they become incidents and affect customer experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Health modeling is an observability exercise that combines business context with raw monitoring data to quantify the overall health of a workload, helping set a baseline and detect drift from expected operational states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4aefadf5c38a99059d5cac5297d2b1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observability">
  <data key="d0">Observability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Observability is a concept focused on robust and contextualized instrumentation and monitoring to provide critical insight into application health.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability at component level and aggregated across correlated user flows provides a holistic view of system health status.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability provides meaningful alerting and supports incident response through logs, metrics, and telemetry data.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability enables visibility into systems, data-driven decisions, proactive maintenance, and capacity planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability refers to operations built for proactive maintenance, quality and security assurance, capacity planning, and product management.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability serves operational excellence by monitoring health events and validating workload design to inform future development.&lt;SEP&gt;Observability ensures meaningful alerting and successful incident response for a workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be641287d1772cdb4176dc9a5df85b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeefe2d63573562646e740d09fa6d491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Score">
  <data key="d0">Health Score</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A granular score calculated automatically from underlying metrics to represent the health of application components and user flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layered Application Health">
  <data key="d0">Layered Application Health</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A top-down design approach that defines application health in layered, measurable format by quantifying healthy and unhealthy states across components and user flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Level Objective">
  <data key="d0">Service Level Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service Level Objective (SLO) is a target for availability attainment calculated using the health model.&lt;SEP&gt;SLO is a target for availability attainment, calculated using the health model to distinguish service degradation from unavailability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Flows">
  <data key="d0">User Flows</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User flows are mapped paths through an application whose health states are aggregated to represent overall application health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0de195b0afed20e3d851a968d363d0ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979829</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log Analytics Workspace">
  <data key="d0">Log Analytics Workspace</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Log Analytics workspace serves as the core Azure-native data sink to store and analyze operational data.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics workspace is a resource for storing logs and enabling data collection and querying capabilities, deployed into a specified Azure region.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics workspace is a unified data sink for operational data in Azure Monitor, supporting query storage, data retention, and cross-workspace queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Log Analytics Workspace is used for ingesting and analyzing activity logs from Microsoft Entra and other sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aee778ccfa3886c52f485cafeef0009b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dedicated Clusters">
  <data key="d0">Dedicated Clusters</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedicated Clusters are a deployment option enabling Availability Zones for protection from zone failures, requiring a minimum daily data ingest commitment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979829</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Packs">
  <data key="d0">Query Packs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Query packs are Azure Resource Manager resources containing log queries as JSON that can be shared across subscriptions and stored externally.&lt;SEP&gt;Query packs are Azure Resource Manager resources containing queries as JSON, used to protect and recover log queries if the Log Analytics workspace is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7255c274585b0f1f482e338bbc6c26aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Databricks">
  <data key="d0">Azure Databricks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Databricks is an analytical technology that can be integrated into Azure Synapse pipelines for additional Spark capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Databricks is an Azure service with abstracted capacity models that automatically distribute workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Cognitive Services">
  <data key="d0">Azure Cognitive Services</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Cognitive Services solves general problems in various domains such as anomaly detection, usable in Azure Synapse and Databricks.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Cognitive Services offers predictive capabilities with low administrative and integration overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6891eb227254197568b44bf03596d7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure ML">
  <data key="d0">Azure ML</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure ML is a machine learning service integrated with Synapse Analytics through notebooks for training models using Automated ML.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4678f659d2199619f053d40287ff2e4a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776979830</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
