</node>
<node id="Azure Resource Manager">
  <data key="d0">Azure Resource Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Resource Manager is the deployment and management framework under which query packs are managed as resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager provides an API and control plane through which most Azure operational actions are exposed and accessible.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager is a management control plane in Azure that Azure Policy is part of.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Resource Manager (ARM) is the control plane that Azure Policy supplements to restrict actions authorized users can perform.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bc4a6aa7dad91160ab49f8c99c2ea47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a324803e46dec295e5d9abb5a43f8a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bb2c831e41151a23a478ec8c59ab787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8deba810ca14d9b278b1f9d887802f2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-health-modeling.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-operational-procedures.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776980105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Standard Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Azure Standard Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Standard Load Balancer is an Azure load balancing SKU designed for internal traffic distribution, providing a 99.99% SLA across Availability Zones. Unlike the Basic SKU, it is backed by an SLA, making it suitable for production workloads requiring high availability.

Azure Standard Load Balancer also provides cross-region routing capabilities for managing global traffic. However, its Cross-Region feature is in preview with technical limitations and is not recommended for mission-critical workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc31ff972bb32047bd652b7c4ab8132</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983283</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure DNS">
  <data key="d0">Azure DNS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure DNS is a shared foundational service serving as a global platform dependency for almost all Azure services.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS is a global Azure service with automatic redundancy across multiple regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS is a global service providing public and private zone name resolution with built-in zone and geo redundancy, resilient to regional outages.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure DNS is a shared foundational service serving as a global platform dependency for almost all Azure services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86188fe80b60fb0b86bacfbd8970add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/redundancy.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Web Application Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Azure Web Application Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) can be deployed on Azure Front Door for traffic inspection.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) can be deployed on Azure Front Door at network edge locations to inspect every incoming request, supporting built-in and custom rules in detection or prevention mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall blocks most DDoS threats and protects ingress traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) can be deployed on Azure Front Door for traffic inspection.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) can be deployed on Azure Front Door at network edge locations to inspect every incoming request, supporting built-in and custom rules in detection or prevention mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce015784fd1d8129dac8c9bbf32bf565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Global Backbone Network">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Global Backbone Network</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Microsoft global backbone network is used by Azure Front Door for optimized connectivity between edge nodes and backends.&lt;SEP&gt;The Microsoft global backbone network is used by Azure Front Door for optimized connectivity between edge nodes and backends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Traffic Routing">
  <data key="d0">Global Traffic Routing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global traffic routing is the practice of distributing traffic across multiple active regional deployment stamps using a global routing service.&lt;SEP&gt;Global traffic routing is the practice of distributing traffic across multiple active regional deployment stamps using a global routing service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multicloud Active-Active Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Multicloud Active-Active Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A multicloud active-active deployment approach provides broader redundancy to global outage scenarios but introduces significant operational complexities.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach using active stamps across two or more cloud providers with redundant third-party routing for global routing, though not recommended due to operational complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;A multicloud active-active deployment approach provides broader redundancy to global outage scenarios but introduces significant operational complexities.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach using active stamps across two or more cloud providers with redundant third-party routing for global routing, though not recommended due to operational complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a9b32aa690001ea5387c320074295c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anycast Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Anycast Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Anycast protocol is used by Azure Front Door with split TCP for optimized global connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Anycast protocol is used by Azure Front Door with split TCP for optimized global connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ff5c56a565c7a13e4cc5066c5ed0775</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Application Gateway">
  <data key="d0">Azure Application Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Application Gateway provides WAF capabilities within each region for the Traffic Manager ingress path.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway provides WAF capabilities within each regional deployment stamp.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway is a regional Azure service providing WAF capabilities for ingress traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway is a replica-aware load balancing service.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway provides WAF capabilities within each region for the Traffic Manager ingress path.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway provides WAF capabilities within each regional deployment stamp.&lt;SEP&gt;Azure Application Gateway is a regional Azure service providing WAF capabilities for ingress traffic.</data>
