</node>
<node id="Session Affinity">
  <data key="d0">Session Affinity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Session Affinity uses client-side cookies to route subsequent requests to the same backend as the first request.&lt;SEP&gt;Session Affinity ties requests to specific backends and can negatively impact traffic distribution balance; not recommended for stateless applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Session Affinity uses client-side cookies to route subsequent requests to the same backend as the first request.&lt;SEP&gt;Session Affinity ties requests to specific backends and can negatively impact traffic distribution balance; not recommended for stateless applications.</data>
