</node>
<node id="Azure Firewall">
  <data key="d0">Azure Firewall</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure Firewall is a network security service in Microsoft Azure that requires a dedicated subnet for deployment. It provides security capabilities to secure network egress and control outbound traffic flows, enabling organizations to filter, restrict, and inspect outbound internet traffic from resources such as Virtual Machines. Azure Firewall can be deployed as a dedicated resource or as a centrally shared resource. Additionally, it helps mitigate port exhaustion issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bdc71fab10e8d772205c8ac9acd6546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c136188a7c5b35c34dacbc95825b4191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ee1cd59b7faad09ea96a1e39a65bcd</data>
