<node id="Availability Zone">
  <data key="d0">Availability Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An Availability Zone is a physically separate data center location within an Azure region providing fault isolation, with guaranteed sub-2ms inter-zone latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability zones are separate groups of datacenters within a region with independent power, cooling, and networking infrastructure, designed for high availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability zones are distinct physical locations within an Azure region that provide redundancy and fault isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;An availability zone is an isolated datacenter location within an Azure region that provides resiliency against outages.&lt;SEP&gt;A physically separate zone within an Azure region used for deploying resources with resiliency considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;An Availability Zone is a physically separate data center location within an Azure region providing fault isolation, with guaranteed sub-2ms inter-zone latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd5df507c6d7ae6d803dce8c99d84eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
