<node id="DDoS Attack">
  <data key="d0">DDoS Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distributed Denial of Service attacks render targeted resources unavailable by overwhelming them with illegitimate traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) is a type of malicious attack that represents a failure mode for workloads.&lt;SEP&gt;A distributed denial-of-service attack that can disrupt services, with L3/L4 protection managed by Microsoft and L7 attacks posing residual risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributed Denial of Service attacks render targeted resources unavailable by overwhelming them with illegitimate traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6ee1b46c13062b2f84bc4bd8740f6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f771a609846ef0b7b2580d4b2e3191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86643535bbddea59b9f2b171ec6790db</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/failure-mode-analysis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983280</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Micro-Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Micro-Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A network security design pattern used to isolate and secure individual application workloads based on a Zero Trust model.&lt;SEP&gt;A network security design pattern used to isolate and secure individual application workloads based on a Zero Trust model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Security Groups">
  <data key="d0">Network Security Groups</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NSGs provide IP ACLs for securing ingress paths and isolating application components at subnet or network interface level.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups are used to micro-segment application traffic and enforce security rules on subnets.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Security Groups are used to filter and restrict network traffic and access between subnets.&lt;SEP&gt;NSGs provide IP ACLs for securing ingress paths and isolating application components at subnet or network interface level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0151994e0d96a2045a761ce543e6d2a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero Trust">
  <data key="d0">Zero Trust</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A security model that limits network traffic between workloads based on strict access policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a Microsoft security model providing a proactive and integrated approach to applying security across all layers of an application, centered on eliminating trust and enforcing verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a security model that assumes a breached state and verifies each request as though it originates from an uncontrolled network.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a security model that requires explicit verification, least-privilege access, and assuming breach of security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Zero Trust is a security approach that treats all processes and operations as potential attack vectors.&lt;SEP&gt;A security model that limits network traffic between workloads based on strict access policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31cf91ba30eab331729c73c4002b505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6c19c90a7ec75e7d95d807c1817fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9406ed2aa903d9c51a1e6e1d68aee2dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f391cc5c3fa628d6f44144e1bef0b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-security.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Policies">
  <data key="d0">Network Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Kubernetes specification defining access policies for communication between pods, enforced using ordered rules and label selectors.&lt;SEP&gt;A Kubernetes specification defining access policies for communication between pods, enforced using ordered rules and label selectors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-defd991d185ed0d546fc2887007b9160</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-networking-connectivity.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776983286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Node Pools">
  <data key="d0">Node Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Node pools in AKS allow separation of workloads using nodes with different hardware and software characteristics, but do not provide network-level isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;Node pools in AKS allow separation of workloads using nodes with different hardware and software characteristics, but do not provide network-level isolation.</data>
