</node>
<node id="Confidential-Compute">
  <data key="d0">Confidential-Compute</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidential-compute functionality is a specialized compute capability supporting encryption at rest and in transit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981231</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SDLC">
  <data key="d0">SDLC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SDLC (Software Development Lifecycle) requires security validation that usually needs specialized tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Software Development Lifecycle, a framework of practices that may need to evolve as workloads and external factors change.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Masking">
  <data key="d0">Data Masking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data masking is a compliance guideline practice where specific segments of logs or tabular data are redacted to protect confidentiality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inspection Security Controls">
  <data key="d0">Inspection Security Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security controls like firewalls and content safety filters that add latency by performing verification on data flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity Controls">
  <data key="d0">Identity Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security controls requiring explicit verification of each invocation, consuming compute cycles and network resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981232</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encryption And Decryption">
  <data key="d0">Encryption And Decryption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryptographic operations requiring dedicated compute cycles, with overhead correlated to algorithm complexity and IV generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logging">
  <data key="d0">Logging</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of recording system events, which impacts system resources and network bandwidth as extensiveness increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Resource Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Architectural practice that introduces network hops in a workload's architecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Misconfiguration">
  <data key="d0">Misconfiguration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Incorrect or overextended security control configuration that can negatively impact performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Web Application Firewalls">
  <data key="d0">Web Application Firewalls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Firewalls that perform deep packet inspection, which can affect performance when inspecting irrelevant languages or platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="File Integrity Monitors">
  <data key="d0">File Integrity Monitors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security tools that monitor file changes and can cause lock contention if key files are not excluded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981233</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Latency">
  <data key="d0">Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Latency is the delay added to requests by security controls such as inspection, identity verification, and encryption in workload flows.&lt;SEP&gt;Increased time introduced by gateway routing, messaging brokers, or anti-corruption layers that draws against performance target budgets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c68f04b50833c59213a11d31e461972</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Firewalls">
  <data key="d0">Firewalls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Firewalls are inspection security controls that add latency and can impact performance through rule ordering, complexity, and quantity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virus Scanners">
  <data key="d0">Virus Scanners</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Virus scanners are security tools that can cause lock contention if key files are not excluded from scanning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bdb47b7b9b6deb20ca5a8f3b43597b66</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Testing Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Performance Testing Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategy for conducting various types of performance tests including manual, low-effort tests and automated routine performance tests in pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981261</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Gates">
  <data key="d0">Quality Gates</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Checkpoints that ensure each stage of deployment meets performance standards before moving forward, such as blocking a release if performance falls below expectations.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality gates enforce best practices to reduce risks, with artifacts gaining confidence each time they pass through a gate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981373</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacity Planning">
  <data key="d0">Capacity Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Planning based on performance models and capability of selected resources, using predictive modeling to forecast anticipated changes in capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning involves proactively measuring and provisioning resources to address anticipated demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning is a key strategy for performance efficiency that involves planning resource supply to meet demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning is one of the purposes served by operations built for observability.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacity planning is one of the purposes for which observability operations are built.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proof Of Concept">
  <data key="d0">Proof Of Concept</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A validation approach to confirm proposed design choices can meet performance targets and anticipated load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981261</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Model">
  <data key="d0">Performance Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A model that is updated based on tested and monitored metrics, indicating increased, reduced, or no effect on performance of flows.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance model considers usage patterns, business impact, and operational costs to calculate initial performance targets and supports strategic resource planning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981262</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Techniques used to forecast anticipated changes in capacity, helping avoid resource shortages or overprovisioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981262</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Well-Architected Pillars">
  <data key="d0">Azure Well-Architected Pillars</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A framework whose optimizations in various pillars can cause changes that strain workload resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981262</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The evaluation of scaling needs for prioritized flows based on usage requirements and expected demand patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Dynamic scaling evaluates elasticity needs for prioritized flows based on usage requirements and expected demand patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of dynamically adjusting capacity by scaling up when demand increases and scaling down when no longer needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f94fd9e9c0fb3fcb2d643d3e9f97a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Efficiency Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Performance Efficiency Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Performance Efficiency checklist is used to validate workload design against performance efficiency principles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Performance Efficiency checklist is a recommended next step resource for performance efficiency guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Targets">
  <data key="d0">Performance Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance targets are negotiated benchmarks aligned with business requirements and user experience expectations, refined iteratively through testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a2d53adbb648e8c6193f0ba7b2c4cb67</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Performance Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance optimization is a practice of dedicating time to monitor and continuously improve system performance throughout the development lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nonfunctional Requirements">
  <data key="d0">Nonfunctional Requirements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonfunctional requirements are targets that can be revisited and updated by analyzing historical production trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CDN">
  <data key="d0">CDN</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A CDN (Content Delivery Network) is a component that can optimize the system and improve user experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95903051168953cfcf55ce5d2cf2a23a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981263</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PE:01">
  <data key="d0">PE:01</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PE:01 recommends defining numerical performance targets tied to workload requirements for all workload flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PE:02">
  <data key="d0">PE:02</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PE:02 recommends conducting capacity planning before predicted changes in usage patterns such as seasonal variations, product updates, or marketing campaigns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md</data>
