  <data key="d5">1776981288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PE:10">
  <data key="d0">PE:10</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PE:10 recommends optimizing operational tasks and minimizing their effects on workload performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PE:11">
  <data key="d0">PE:11</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PE:11 recommends planning to respond to live performance issues with clear communication and preventive measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PE:12">
  <data key="d0">PE:12</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PE:12 recommends continuously optimizing performance for components that show deterioration over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design Review Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Design Review Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Design Review Checklist is a structured set of recommendations for Performance Efficiency to help scale systems and meet workload usage demand.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Efficiency Tradeoffs">
  <data key="d0">Performance Efficiency Tradeoffs</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance Efficiency Tradeoffs is a related document exploring other concepts and tradeoffs associated with Performance Efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;A document covering tradeoffs related to the performance efficiency pillar of architecture design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aabe428ecc28c763c7d768871230b9a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c68f04b50833c59213a11d31e461972</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/checklist.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Partitioning And Sharding">
  <data key="d0">Data Partitioning And Sharding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Data partitioning and sharding help avoid performance issues in large datasets but increase complexity due to consistency requirements across additional resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Data partitioning and sharding are techniques that can complicate routine operational tasks like backups and key rotations when teams try to ensure data consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Culture Stress">
  <data key="d0">Culture Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Culture stress is a tradeoff associated with Operational Excellence, relating to impacts on team morale from blame and inconvenient work schedules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd18a4f6bd04d93d17db01be0273b02f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denormalization">
  <data key="d0">Denormalization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Denormalization optimizes data access patterns for performance but introduces complexity from keeping multiple data representations synchronized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Bus">
  <data key="d0">Message Bus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A message bus is used for load leveling, introducing a critical stateful component to the workload.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Load Balancer">
  <data key="d0">Load Balancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A load balancer distributes traffic for autoscaled replicas, requiring reliable operation.&lt;SEP&gt;A load balancer built into zone-redundant services disperses requests across instances in multiple availability zones and redirects traffic during outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application Performance Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Application Performance Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">APM is a system that enables teams to learn from active environments through instrumentation of application code or hosting environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981326</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Defense In Depth">
  <data key="d0">Defense In Depth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Defense in depth is a security approach establishing controls across multiple layers, sometimes redundantly, which may be compromised by performance optimizations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Transactions">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Transactions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthetic transactions are used in performance testing on active environments, carrying the risk of causing malfunctions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94148f63b4b1385b51dfefa8ba2f3472</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Pillar">
  <data key="d0">Security Pillar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security pillar prioritizes strong segmentation to enable fine-grained security controls and reduce blast radius.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security pillar prioritizes a reduced and contained surface area to minimize attack vectors and strong segmentation to support targeted security controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981581</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multitenancy">
  <data key="d0">Multitenancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multitenancy is a scenario of sharing resources through increased density, which can lead to security concerns like unauthorized lateral movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Design Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Performance Design Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance-centric cloud design patterns may introduce extra components to improve performance but add complexity and cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b284d3b10b64577458ddc2798074113b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/performance-efficiency/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring System">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A monitoring system is built with its own stack and flows, decoupled from the workload, covering infrastructure, application health, and build and release processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Telemetry is emitted from application code to correlate key points of execution flow and provide end-to-end views at different granularity levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Metrics are monitoring signals prioritized for triggering actions that rely on numeric measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logs">
  <data key="d0">Logs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Logs are monitoring signals used to provide context for flows and dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981369</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traces">
  <data key="d0">Traces</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Traces are monitoring signals used to provide context for flows and dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Profiles">
  <data key="d0">Profiles</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Profiles are monitoring signals used to get lower-level visibility such as memory allocation into the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dashboards">
  <data key="d0">Dashboards</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dashboards aggregate and visualize monitoring data for different audiences, including situational dashboards and operational dashboards with drill-down capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerts are actionable notifications with standardized descriptions and severity levels, triggered only for incidents requiring action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incident Management">
  <data key="d0">Incident Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Incident management is a cross-functional skill provided by centralized operations teams to handle workload incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;Incident management is a reactive cycle that efficient monitoring aims to reduce by anticipating issues before they affect customer experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Business Data">
  <data key="d0">Business Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Business data is explicitly out of scope for observability implementations and is protected from disruption by monitoring configuration changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ea3d1c60d4f024bf104694fc558f794</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981370</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Excellence Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Operational Excellence Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Operational Excellence checklist is a resource used to drive action after setting operational strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operational Excellence checklist is a recommended resource for exploring additional operational excellence concepts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A/B Testing">
  <data key="d0">A/B Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A/B testing is an experimentation mechanism used to encourage innovation while keeping costs low.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agile Practices">
  <data key="d0">Agile Practices</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Agile development practices focus on action optimization, leading to shorter release lifecycles and earlier issue detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shift Left">
  <data key="d0">Shift Left</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shift left refers to detecting and resolving issues earlier in operations for manual and automated processes, deployment, quality assurance, and observability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Operations Teams">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Operations Teams</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized operations teams provide specialized skills and breadth of experience, offering cross-functional support such as incident management and monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Centralized operations teams provide shared resources with specialized skills and cross-functional expertise including incident management and monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db85d35bad38238654d528c03dcdbee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Improvement">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Improvement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous improvement is a goal driven by learning from experience and collected data to iteratively enhance workload operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transparent Communication">
  <data key="d0">Transparent Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparent communication is promoted through common systems and tools, enabling situational awareness across teams and environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blameless Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Blameless Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blameless analysis involves conducting post-release and post-incident reviews to identify areas for improvement without assigning blame.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06fa22ab48be5657235d1672d0089037</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safe Deployment Practices">
  <data key="d0">Safe Deployment Practices</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Safe deployment practices aim to achieve consistency in deployments using guardrails that reduce the effect of errors and unexpected conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Safe deployment practices involve deploying multiple concurrent instances to shift traffic in a controlled way, increasing resource costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Safe deployment practices (SDP) are processes and procedures that define how to safely make and deploy changes to a workload, focusing on managing risk and minimizing human error.&lt;SEP&gt;Safe deployment practices encompass automation, IaC, branching strategies, feature flags, and progressive exposure rollout.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Pipelines">
  <data key="d0">Automated Pipelines</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated pipelines deploy code and infrastructure changes across all environments to ensure consistent and repeatable deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Progressive Exposure">
  <data key="d0">Progressive Exposure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Progressive exposure is a deployment pattern that allows gradual rollout of new features and controlled adoption by users.&lt;SEP&gt;Progressive exposure is a gradual rollout deployment model that minimizes the potential blast radius of deployment-caused issues by deploying to successively larger groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02d45413152a840f1fd2444de10c78fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration Drift">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Drift</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuration drift is a deviation from desired infrastructure state that IaC helps detect and mitigate.</data>
