<node id="Canary Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Canary Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Canary deployments are a progressive exposure model where a small group receives the new feature first before rolling out to larger groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/safe-deployments.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Flags">
  <data key="d0">Feature Flags</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature flags selectively enable or disable new features in production, allowing controlled exposure and quick rollback.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature flags are used to enable new versions for target users in canary deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature flags are a practice used to create, change, and deploy features in a controlled manner.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44641efcd9d3edd6dd3a0ceda8c1536b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082de75994ad13c747e8ee30b159eda8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a688a846e77a6107a53c8f43220265c2</data>
