<node id="Return On Investment">
  <data key="d0">Return On Investment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Return on investment (ROI) is a financial metric that architecture design must factor in alongside financial constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Return on investment (ROI) is a measure of business value that cost optimization aims to maximize for workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21e41edd72b9157b512d1a210db4941b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/checklist.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Model">
  <data key="d0">Cost Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A cost model is a fundamental exercise that segments expenses and estimates total cost of ownership, including infrastructure, support, and implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FinOps">
  <data key="d0">FinOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FinOps refers to organizational financial operations practices that workload costs should align with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
