</node>
<node id="Accountability Model">
  <data key="d0">Accountability Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An accountability model is an effective but flexible governance structure with properly assigned roles and responsibilities to enforce functional expectations and prevent unnecessary expenditure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Baseline">
  <data key="d0">Cost Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A cost baseline includes projected growth and ensures design choices work within allocated budget to meet functional and nonfunctional requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-475405476dbc7b00e7119497a7834c18</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Showback">
  <data key="d0">Showback</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Showback is a process for reporting and attributing costs to business units without direct billing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chargeback">
  <data key="d0">Chargeback</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chargeback is a process for directly billing business units for their resource consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Right-Sizing">
  <data key="d0">Right-Sizing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Right-sizing involves adjusting resource allocation to match actual usage, reducing costs by resizing or removing underutilized resources or changing SKUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Cost Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost alerts are proactive notifications implemented when spending approaches predefined budget thresholds to prevent budget overruns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dcd6623608bb76388ae9e58c2350270b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Usage Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Design For Usage Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design principle focused on maximizing the use of resources and operations to meet functional and nonfunctional requirements of a solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design For Rate Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Design For Rate Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A design principle focused on increasing efficiency without redesigning or sacrificing requirements, by optimizing utility and costs of existing resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor And Optimize Over Time">
  <data key="d0">Monitor And Optimize Over Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle of continuously right-sizing investment as workloads evolve with the ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active Model">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where all provisioned resources are actively used, preferred over active-passive to avoid idle resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumption-Based Pricing">
  <data key="d0">Consumption-Based Pricing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A billing model where users pay for what they use, suitable when resources are not expected to be fully utilized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fixed-Price Billing">
  <data key="d0">Fixed-Price Billing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A billing model that usually costs less when utilization is high and predictable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981521</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Model">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where some provisioned resources remain idle as standby, which can lead to underutilization of paid resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dfd30e89a4e9aae78702c1f5f2ad501</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/principles.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981521</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
