</node>
<node id="Active-Active Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region deployment where multiple regions actively process requests simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive Deployments">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive Deployments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region deployment designating one primary region with secondary regions for failover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Residency">
  <data key="d0">Data Residency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data residency refers to restrictions on physical locations where data can be stored and processed, often driven by legal or regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Data residency is an architectural concern about where data is stored, which varies by deployment approach and region selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Data residency compliance is achieved in both zonal and zone-redundant deployments by storing data in the selected Azure region.&lt;SEP&gt;Data residency refers to compliance requirements about where data is stored geographically.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance concern regarding where data is physically stored, important for regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Data residency is a regulatory requirement mandating that data must remain in a specific location, critically important for healthcare and banking applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3c83649acd71df5d7f58cf6c4f1629c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981734</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proseware, Inc.">
  <data key="d0">Proseware, Inc.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Proseware, Inc. is a SaaS company that builds software used by companies around the world, with a geographically distributed user base.&lt;SEP&gt;Proseware, Inc. builds software used by companies worldwide with a geographically distributed user base.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Zone Multi-Region Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Zone Multi-Region Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach combining multiple availability zones and multiple regions for high reliability and data residency compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach combining zone-redundant components with replication across multiple regions for the highest reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure NetApp Files">
  <data key="d0">Azure NetApp Files</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure NetApp Files supports cross-zone replication for data redundancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed83bb2fdd642ffb5c3592b2c8243758</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locally Redundant Deployments With Backup Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Locally Redundant Deployments With Backup Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach that extends locally redundant deployment by performing regular backups of infrastructure and data to a secondary region for extra protection against primary region outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonal Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Zonal Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A zonal (pinned) deployment model where a resource is deployed into a specific availability zone.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment model where a resource is deployed into a specific availability zone.&lt;SEP&gt;Zonal deployment is an approach where resources are deployed into specific availability zones, requiring manual failover handling during outages.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach where resources are deployed to a specific availability zone, sometimes known as zone-pinned deployment, which reduces latency between components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67203c92bdb0aa325b8ab2d546d9ef56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Passive">
  <data key="d0">Active-Passive</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture in which one primary instance processes traffic and secondary instances serve traffic if the primary is unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;A traffic routing approach where one instance handles traffic while others remain on standby for failover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active-Active">
  <data key="d0">Active-Active</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An architecture in which multiple instances of a solution actively process requests at the same time.&lt;SEP&gt;A request distribution model where multiple instances simultaneously handle traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981739</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metro DR">
  <data key="d0">Metro DR</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An active-passive deployment across multiple availability zones within a region, also known as in-region DR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-771f5e6a7f069d0317878849e102ccc7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Regions">
  <data key="d0">Azure Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Geographic perimeters containing sets of datacenters used for deploying Azure solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where resources are deployed into multiple Azure regions.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach that distributes resources across multiple regions, offering high reliability at high cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-region deployment is an approach where workloads are deployed across multiple Azure regions for higher reliability and geographic proximity to users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locally Redundant Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Locally Redundant Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment model where a resource is deployed into a single region without reference to an availability zone.&lt;SEP&gt;A deployment approach where resources are deployed without specifying multiple availability zones or regions, offering low cost and low reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac69076e8ebd4d001c0267c2edca19ed</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Regions">
  <data key="d0">Paired Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A relationship between two Azure regions connected to enable specific types of multi-region solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981742</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Datacenter">
  <data key="d0">Datacenter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A facility containing servers, networking equipment, and other hardware to support Azure resources and workloads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f88755bbf9fb155be427dfc8a8708cc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Region">
  <data key="d0">Paired Region</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired regions support certain types of multi-region deployment approaches in Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shared Responsibility Principle">
  <data key="d0">Shared Responsibility Principle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle describing how responsibilities are divided between the cloud provider and the customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981743</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platform As A Service">
  <data key="d0">Platform As A Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Platform as a service (PaaS) solutions typically support zone-redundant deployments in Azure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba037f30d06665208af1b780fac7d88b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Data Replication">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Data Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Asynchronous data replication is a method where changes are committed in the primary region and replicated to secondary regions later, minimizing latency impact but risking some data loss during outages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synchronous Data Replication">
  <data key="d0">Synchronous Data Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Synchronous data replication requires write operations to complete in each Azure region before a transaction is considered complete, providing very high reliability but potentially low performance due to inter-region latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Region Network Latency">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Region Network Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-region network latency is the delay in data transmission between geographically separated regions, significantly affecting solution design.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Region Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Region Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-region architecture involves deploying solutions across multiple Azure regions for resilience, with trade-offs in cost, performance, and operational complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Azure Region Pairs">
  <data key="d0">Azure Region Pairs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azure region pairs are paired Azure regions where some services automatically replicate data between them.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Object Replication">
  <data key="d0">Object Replication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Object replication is an Azure Storage feature that can be used to replicate data across regions when geo-redundant storage is not available.&lt;SEP&gt;Object replication is an Azure Storage feature that can be used as an alternative when GRS is not available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Zone Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Zone Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-zone architecture involves deploying zone-redundant components within a region, and can be combined with multi-region approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e92839392c86e80753e5e62c70459c56</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
