  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fourth Coffee">
  <data key="d0">Fourth Coffee</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Fourth Coffee is a small business developing an internal timesheet application with cost efficiency as a primary concern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fabrikam, Inc.">
  <data key="d0">Fabrikam, Inc.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Fabrikam, Inc. is a company migrating a legacy application from on-premises to Azure using an IaaS approach based on VMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lamna Healthcare Company">
  <data key="d0">Lamna Healthcare Company</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Lamna Healthcare Company is implementing an electronic health record system on Azure with strict data residency requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Woodgrove Bank">
  <data key="d0">Woodgrove Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Woodgrove Bank runs mission-critical core banking operations on Azure with very low risk tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonal (Pinned) Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Zonal (Pinned) Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach where resources are pinned to a specific availability zone, with passive deployments across other zones for in-region DR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locally Redundant Deployment With Backups Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Locally Redundant Deployment With Backups Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A low-cost deployment approach with significant risks, using local redundancy and cross-region backups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone-Redundant Deployment With Backup Across Regions">
  <data key="d0">Zone-Redundant Deployment With Backup Across Regions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deployment approach providing multiple layers of resiliency with high performance through zone redundancy and cross-region backups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reliability Hub">
  <data key="d0">Reliability Hub</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reliability Hub is an Azure resource providing guidance on specific deployment options and approaches for each Azure service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e0b79907727407bf3c0d7f73778f8c4f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service-Level Objective">
  <data key="d0">Service-Level Objective</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A service-level objective (SLO) represents the expected uptime target for a solution, such as 99.9% uptime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geodes Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Geodes Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Geodes pattern is an approach for deploying workloads across multiple regions to bring applications closer to users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/design-guides/regions-availability-zones.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1776981747</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Tolerance">
  <data key="d0">Risk Tolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk tolerance refers to the varying degrees of acceptable risk within organizations, differing by workload and influencing resiliency strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0ea658bc5677a379a1105409b6be36f</data>
