<edge source="Operational Excellence" target="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Operational Excellence practices can increase resource costs, reduce delivery focus, and increase tooling demands, creating tradeoffs with Cost Optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Operational Excellence has tradeoffs with Cost Optimization regarding workload return on investment.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost optimization can compromise SDLC capacities, reduce observability, and defer maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d9">compromised SDLC,deferred maintenance,delivery focus,reduced observability,resource spending,tooling,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-31da0f57b1bbfcf80aeba441d56d15f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9454754aa8d04d2fcd10f9b4227d89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1d75683e73385fab74d25019f702cd</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/operational-excellence/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
