<edge source="Security" target="SIEM">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Security monitoring uses SIEM tooling to track security events and respond to incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;SIEM tools support security through aggregation and threat intelligence capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d9">incident response,monitoring,observability,threat intelligence</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776981236</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Security" target="Cost Optimization">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Maximizing reliability and security has cost implications that must be balanced against business requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Security requires additional infrastructure and premium resources that increase costs, creating tradeoffs with cost optimization goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Security measures increase costs through premium SKUs, log storage, resource consumption, and operational processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cost optimization can lead to reduced security controls, creating tradeoffs with security posture.</data>
  <data key="d9">additional infrastructure,design tradeoffs,increased costs,increased demand,tradeoff</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a3f13da121cb986a81d213029e9150d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2cc133f2276ccf7c79c3147bf59683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c503260b531691857650e03a6b6b239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ce425f3646f4ada6cca51a61f53897</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/mission-critical/mission-critical-design-principles.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/security/tradeoffs.md&lt;SEP&gt;/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/cost-optimization/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776981585</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Security" target="Replication">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Replication increases the workload surface area, which conflicts with the security goal of minimizing attack vectors.</data>
  <data key="d9">surface area increase</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3d1a3bf99f17f7553d47f5ea8122843f</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/abossard/Desktop/cxe/well-architected/well-architected/reliability/tradeoffs.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1776980960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Security" target="Disaster Recovery">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Disaster recovery solutions increase surface area and require implementation of additional security controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Security controls affect recovery time objectives and must be included in disaster recovery plans.</data>
